{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787313693147329001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"despotic-prime-reindeer","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"270348acd1960af70b5b63311d5c90c5481756e7212fa1c707978da8de316d26","event_uuid":"36cc5356-457e-460c-b534-f12748587d9e","position":{"commit_sha":"df0509814cdeffff194eaac901ebdcdbf4b47318","position":"1787308882729976001-36cc5356-457e-460c-b534-f12748587d9e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0d50d46b9432bf80c5a1afd75823fe5d192b83a38c8e7d0dcd7544efb55668d6","event_uuid":"cda11ca5-b9e3-4a49-b7d1-f8f68fd50bdf","position":{"commit_sha":"997203c70c42406d0c5d86b5d8838cb31f156f69","position":"1787308911499734001-cda11ca5-b9e3-4a49-b7d1-f8f68fd50bdf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787308882729976001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"cda11ca5-b9e3-4a49-b7d1-f8f68fd50bdf","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"96db-365e-f2c3-4547"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe parent-first cascade (`docs/concurrency.md` §I4a) is implemented ONLY in\n`transition_compute` / `claim_compute`. The Jira reconciler's inbound-apply path writes\nSTATUS events **directly**, bypassing that seam entirely:\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py:322`\n(`_inbound_update_write_status_event`) and `:149` (`_inbound_create_write_status_event`)\nboth call `_write_event_file(tracker_dir, local_id, \"STATUS\", ...)`.\n\nSo an inbound Jira status change that moves a child into an active status does NOT pull\nits ancestors along, and can compose exactly the invalid states I4a forbids — a `closed`\nparent holding an `open`/`in_progress` child, or an `open` parent holding an\n`in_progress` child.\n\nThis is a **parity gap on the automated-caller surface**, found by the Step-7 parity\ncensus while fixing `paragonite-fruited-minnow` (96db-365e-f2c3-4547). It is NOT\nintroduced by that fix and is NOT specific to one edge: the reconciler has never applied\nthe cascade on ANY of the three cascading edges, including the two that already shipped.\n\n## Scope note\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/**` was held by another agent during the debug\nsession that found this, so nothing was changed there.\n\n## Open design question (answer before implementing)\nWhether the inbound path SHOULD cascade is a genuine design decision, not an obvious\nyes: inbound apply deliberately re-materialises a peer's recorded state, which is closer\nto the `cascade=False` replay contract than to an interactive client write. Two candidate\nanswers:\n1. Route inbound status through the cascading seam, so the local store never holds an\n   I4a-invalid state regardless of what Jira says.\n2. Declare inbound apply an explicit `cascade=False`-equivalent surface and document that\n   I4a is a contract on INTERACTIVE writes only, with `fsck` (or a reconcile-time audit)\n   as the detector for states arriving from a peer.\n\nOption 2 may well be right, but today the behaviour is undocumented either way, which is\nthe actual defect.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A decision is recorded for whether inbound reconcile applies the parent-first cascade.\n- [ ] `docs/concurrency.md` §I4a states explicitly which write surfaces the invariant binds\n      (interactive only, or all), so the reconciler's behaviour is no longer undocumented.\n- [ ] If option 1: an inbound status change into an active status cascades to eligible\n      ancestors, with a test driving the inbound-apply path (not `transition_compute`).\n- [ ] If option 2: a test pins the non-cascading behaviour as intended, and the detector\n      for peer-originated invalid states is named.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"bb73-97de-eeea-4899","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Inbound reconcile writes STATUS directly, bypassing the parent-first cascade","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["36cc5356-457e-460c-b534-f12748587d9e","cda11ca5-b9e3-4a49-b7d1-f8f68fd50bdf"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787313693147329001,"uuid":"91ac37ea-c0fb-40c5-9062-15ba47b16152"}